{
 "_comment": [
  "Nominative Lithuanian place names, used to verify a birthplace",
  "recovered from 1996-1999 biography prose.",
  "",
  "Those pages print the birthplace in the locative ('Kaune', 'Klaipėdoje',",
  "'Šiaulių rajone') while the rest of the corpus stores the nominative.",
  "Suffix rules alone cannot do the conversion -- '-yje' yields both",
  "Panevėžys and Radviliškis -- so candidates generated by those rules are",
  "accepted only if they appear here. That lookup is what makes the",
  "conversion safe: a mis-parsed fragment produces no candidate in this",
  "list and is dropped rather than written.",
  "",
  "GENERATED. Do not hand-edit: scripts/build_place_vocabulary.py --check",
  "is run by tests/test_place_vocabulary.py and will fail.",
  "",
  "Derived from gimimo-vieta across the 49 non-archive elections, keeping",
  "values seen 3+ times that are shaped like a name rather than a",
  "questionnaire answer: 335 entries, from 1,464 frequent-enough values",
  "among 23,258 distinct ones.",
  "",
  "What it does today is small, and deliberately so. When issue #63 built",
  "this, the archive card's own 'Gimimo vieta' was not being read and the",
  "biography was those records' only birthplace; issue #69 recovered the",
  "card field, and 873 of the 950 archive records now take it from there.",
  "This vocabulary serves the 39 with no card birthplace whose biography",
  "names a place, resolving 19 of them -- 9 through a multi-word nominative",
  "('Krasnojarsko kraštas', 'Vilniaus rajonas'). The other 20 are villages,",
  "parishes and Soviet-era regions no lookup would settle.",
  "",
  "The header used to claim '1,357 of 21,951 distinct names, which resolves",
  "454 of the archive's 571 birthplaces against 465'. None of those five",
  "figures was reproducible -- the file held 1,100 entries at its own",
  "commit -- and the 454 described the era before #69 (issue #155)."
 ],
